        {
          "id": "cookingNote",
          "type": "note",
          "lines": [
            {
              "b": "Cooking — instructions:",
              "t": ""
            },
            "Heat-Treatment: QA personnel will take the time and temperature of the meat before and after it goes into the oven.",
            "Cooking: QA personnel will test the internal temperature of the thickest (coldest spot) piece of meat using a thermapen and note the temperature once it comes out of the oven. Internal temperature of meat ≥ 160 °F."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "coolingNote",
          "type": "note",
          "lines": [
            {
              "b": "Cooling — instructions:",
              "t": ""
            },
            "Stabilization: QA personnel will test the internal temperature of the thickest (warmest spot) piece using a thermapen and note the temperature once it comes out of the oven.",
            "1. Precooling: 10-15 min after cooking/heat treatment, record time and temperature. Temperature should be above 130°F.",
            "2. 1st Stage Cooling: Record time and temperature every 30 min × 3. Temperature needs to be below 80°F by 3rd check.",
            "3. 2nd Stage Cooling: Check time and temperature after 3 hrs from last check.",
            "Stabilization: Temperature from 130°F - 80°F in 1.5 hrs. 80°F - 40°F in 5 hrs. Total cooling time is ≤ 6.5 hrs."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
